\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Keeping a coarse perturbation fixed}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{The identity perturbation in \ref{fdip-01CS} is multiplied
by #{\lambda^{-1}} at each step. When #{0<\lambda<1},
its coefficient grows as the field is blocked. Comparing two
different fine depths at the same coarse depth therefore requires
different starting coefficients. How should the fine coefficient
depend on depth so that a fixed coarse observer sees the same
perturbation?}
